{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"668736a0709b6830bb0f976123c8ef651d7cf6f9"},"timestamp":1511538469,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzY2NTE1Nzc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1994","origin":"github"},"title":"Metadata parsing","message":"Thanks for making Datalad. It looks awesome.\n\nI'm trying to use Datalad for automating document scanning. The plan is to have the documents contain metadata in the form of barcodes that then gets added for the processed files.\nIt seems like Datalad supports parsing metadata from image files, but I couldn't find out how to do this.\nHere's what I tried (with version 0.9.1 of Datalad):\n```\ndatalad create test\ncd test\nmv ../cat.jpg .\ndatalad add cat.jpg\n``` \nI assumed this would have parsed the metadata from the image file, but running\n```\ngit annex metadata cat.jpg\n```\ndoes not return anything.\n\nHow do I parse metadata and how would I add a new parser? Can I just use git annex directly to add the metadata? It seems like Datalad does not have an option for adding bulk metadata as json like git annex does.","files":null}]}